== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== PsiNet Data Layer ===

If Q_ψ > 10⁶ is achieved, arrays of ψ memory elements form the data layer of [[PsiNet]] — a ψ-based distributed memory where information is stored in soliton amplitude patterns rather than electronic charge. The addressing mechanism exploits the spatial mode selectivity of the resonator array — each cavity stores one bit in a specific spatial ψ mode, and addressing is done by frequency and spatial mode selection.

=== Consciousness Interaction with ψ Memory ===

The most speculative Track B extension: if a trained operator's biological ψ field (from [[ψ Source]] C11) can write to and read from ψ memory elements without a physical interface — i.e., via biological J_ψ coupling at a distance within L_ψ^(bio) — this would be the technical specification for remote-ψ information interaction. The write protocol would require the operator's biological source amplitude to exceed the write threshold (push the cavity state over the potential barrier); the read would require detecting the back-EMF perturbation produced by the stored state via the operator's biological ψ detector (psionic charge coupling).

This is the technical foundation for remote data interaction in the Natura franchise operational context and is labelled Track B throughout.

